4. STRADDLE PERTURBATION TEST (was an open question)
==========================================================================
  dual ray slopes sigma = q/p:  sigma_A = 896/1285 = 0.69727626,  sigma_B = 2974400/8847357 = 0.33619080
  'capacity straddle' asks sigma_B < alpha < sigma_A, i.e. alpha in (0.336191, 0.697276)
  intersect with the certificate window alpha > 0.367473:  alpha in (0.367473, 0.697276)
  window width = 0.329803, which contains 3/8, 2/5, 37/100, 7/19, 41/110 and 2457/6592 alike.
  VERDICT: the straddle is NOT decisive.  Do not cite it as evidence for the specific weight.

==========================================================================
5. MULTIPLICATIVE INDEPENDENCE => the linear form never vanishes
==========================================================================
  1285*896   primes: [2, 5, 7, 257]
  8847357*2974400 primes: [2, 3, 5, 11, 13, 2949119]
  primes on the A side only: [7, 257];  on the B side only: [3, 11, 13, 2949119]
  If n*r_A = m*r_B then (1285/896)^n = (8847357/2974400)^m; comparing the
  exponent of 257 forces n = 0, hence m = 0.  So r_A/r_B is IRRATIONAL
  and alpha*r_B - r_A != 0 for every rational alpha: there is always a floor.
  PROVED: True

