==========================================================================
  2457 = {3: 3, 7: 1, 13: 1}      6592 = {2: 6, 103: 1}
  1285 = {5: 1, 257: 1}   896 = {2: 7, 7: 1}
  8847357 = {3: 1, 2949119: 1}   2974400 = {2: 6, 5: 2, 11: 1, 13: 2}
  5872957 (num t_B) = {19: 1, 103: 1, 3001: 1}   11821757 = {31: 1, 381347: 1}
  primes of the weight: [2, 3, 7, 13, 103]
  all of them divide some bias integer: True
  STRIKING: 103 | 6592 AND 103 | 5872957 (the numerator of t_B).
  Heuristic: a random 7-digit integer is divisible by 103 with probability ~1/103 ~ 1%.
  So this is suggestive of a shared construction, NOT proof.  The other
  weight primes (2,3,7,13) are small enough to divide something by chance.
  ACTIONABLE: search constructions whose output ratio is 2457:6592 =
  (3^3*7*13):(2^6*103), with 103 inherited from t_B's numerator.

